[00:01.14] For my own part
[00:02.88] I have never had a thought
[00:04.14] Which I could not set down in words
[00:07.21] With even more distinctness
[00:09.47] Than that with which I conceived it
[00:12.12] There is, however, a class of fancies
[00:15.12] Of exquisite delicacy
[00:17.35] Which are not thoughts
[00:19.56] And to which, as yet, I have found it
[00:21.47] Absolutely impossible
[00:23.19] To adapt to language
[00:25.88] These fancies arise in the soul
[00:29.32] Alas, how rarely
[00:31.22] Only at epochs of most intense tranquility
[00:35.48] When the bodily and mental health
[00:37.68] Are in perfection
[00:39.80] And at those mere points of time
[00:42.50] Where the confines of the waking world
[00:46.06] Blend with the world of dreams
[00:49.73] And so I captured this fancy
[00:53.86] Where all that we see
[00:55.92] Or seem
[00:57.95] Is but a dream
[01:00.05] Within a dream
[01:01.58] 